{ "Identifier":           {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "MMC-SSE-V2.5-I01", "AIMName": "1MMC-SSE-V2.5-I01"},
  "Header":               "MMC-SSE-V2.5",

  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Description":          "Speech Scene Editing. One Speech Scene is open at a time: a Speech Scene arriving is opened, and the first Object added to no open Scene creates one. The User Command places Speech Objects - named as the User names them - (AddedObjects), moves them, changes where they are, takes them out and sets where the Scene is heard from (UserPoV). Every edit is a new version in Shared Storage; a member is held by its identifier and read from Shared Storage when the Scene is output. Outputs: the open Speech Scene, and the User Command, with its response (UserCommandRS) saying how each action was executed.",

